  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "shelley-selected-poems-s0066-p01716",
      "source_en": "In the draft in Nbk 14 p. 21 S. has cancelled a word, which appears to be ‘triumphal’, as BSM v\nsuggests, leaving a gap in the line. 1840 reads ‘trumpet’s’; that might well have been S.’s choice had he\nrevised the draft, as this and the following line refer to the biblical tradition that at the general resur-\nrection the dead will be awakened by the sound of a trumpet: see 1 Corinthians xv 52.\n S. wrote only the word ‘God’, then left the remainder of the line blank. See note to l. 38.",
